{
  "_doc": "Expected first-bad-edge per corpus vector, driven by BOTH language halves. A verdict alone hides an ordering divergence: two verifiers can agree a receipt is unverified while disagreeing about which check failed first, which is the difference between a debuggable report and a guess. Value is the name of the earliest axis in report order that did not PASS, or null when every axis passed.",
